A multi-QPU quantum computing facility is scheduling ten circuit jobs across three quantum processors for the next operational window. The facility director receives the following briefing: QPU-1 is a 20-qubit superconducting processor in a freshly-calibrated state. It has four circuit jobs queued — QC1 (VQE for H2 ground state, scientific priority 5), QC2 (quantum error correction surface code test, priority 8), QC3 (Grover search on a 4-qubit database, priority 4), and QC4 (QAOA Max-Cut benchmark, priority 6). QPU-1's calibration window can accommodate all four circuits. QPU-2 is a 12-qubit ion-trap processor with three circuits queued — QC5 (quantum volume characterization, priority 7), QC6 (Bernstein-Vazirani test, priority 3), QC7 (teleportation fidelity test, priority 5). QPU-2's coherence window can accommodate all three. QPU-3 is a 16-qubit photonic processor with three circuits queued — QC8 (random circuit sampling n=12, priority 4), QC9 (Shor factoring demo, priority 6), QC10 (quantum phase estimation, priority 2). QPU-3 can accommodate all three. Two hardware sharing conflicts exist: QC2 (surface code test on QPU-1) and QC5 (quantum volume on QPU-2) both require the facility's single external quantum error correction decoder unit and cannot run simultaneously; and QC4 (QAOA on QPU-1) sends mid-circuit measurement feedback signals that interfere with QC8's (random circuit sampling on QPU-3) classical control electronics, causing timing violations when both run concurrently. Based only on this operational briefing, infer the binary optimization problem (xi = 1 if circuit QCi runs), identify all constraints, formulate the complete QUBO, and implement a quantum or hybrid workflow that maximizes total scientific priority subject to all QPU capacity and hardware conflict constraints. Report feasible_objective_quality (achieved priority / known optimal 39), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "circuit": "QC1",
      "qpu": "QPU-1",
      "label": "VQE H2 molecule ground state",
      "priority": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "circuit": "QC2",
      "qpu": "QPU-1",
      "label": "Quantum error correction surface code test",
      "priority": 8
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "circuit": "QC3",
      "qpu": "QPU-1",
      "label": "Grover search on 4-qubit database",
      "priority": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "circuit": "QC4",
      "qpu": "QPU-1",
      "label": "QAOA 6-node Max-Cut benchmark",
      "priority": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "circuit": "QC5",
      "qpu": "QPU-2",
      "label": "Quantum volume characterization circuit",
      "priority": 7
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "circuit": "QC6",
      "qpu": "QPU-2",
      "label": "Bernstein-Vazirani hidden string test",
      "priority": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "circuit": "QC7",
      "qpu": "QPU-2",
      "label": "Quantum teleportation fidelity test",
      "priority": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x8",
      "circuit": "QC8",
      "qpu": "QPU-3",
      "label": "Random circuit sampling (n=12)",
      "priority": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x9",
      "circuit": "QC9",
      "qpu": "QPU-3",
      "label": "Shor factoring small integer demo",
      "priority": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x10",
      "circuit": "QC10",
      "qpu": "QPU-3",
      "label": "Quantum phase estimation benchmark",
      "priority": 2
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "qpu_capacity",
      "expression": "x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 <= 4",
      "description": "QPU-1 can execute at most 4 circuits in the current calibration window (all 4 circuits fit)."
    },
    {
      "type": "qpu_capacity",
      "expression": "x5 + x6 + x7 <= 3",
      "description": "QPU-2 can execute at most 3 circuits in the session (all 3 fit)."
    },
    {
      "type": "qpu_capacity",
      "expression": "x8 + x9 + x10 <= 3",
      "description": "QPU-3 can execute at most 3 circuits in the session (all 3 fit)."
    },
    {
      "type": "shared_decoder_conflict",
      "expression": "x2 * x5 = 0",
      "description": "QC2 (surface code test) and QC5 (quantum volume circuit) both require the facility's single classical quantum error correction decoder unit, which cannot serve two QPUs simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "type": "measurement_feedback_conflict",
      "expression": "x4 * x8 = 0",
      "description": "QC4 (QAOA benchmark) sends mid-circuit measurement feedback signals that interfere with QC8's (random circuit sampling) classical control electronics, causing timing violations when both run concurrently."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 10
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_multi_qpu_scheduling():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_priority, scheduled_circuits
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

